==English==
{{Wikiquote}}

===Etymology===
Arabic {{term|مجاهد|sc=Arab|tr=mujáhid}} < [[mu-]] ''one who'' + {{term|جاهد|sc=Arab|tr=jāhada||to wage holy war}} = {{term|جهاد|sc=Arab|tr=jihād||holy war as a religious duty}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|mujahideen}}

# {{Islam}} a [[Muslim]] [[holy]] [[warrior]]

